.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH orbit-postpone 1  "postpone " 
.SH NAME
orbit\-postpone \- Move a task\*(Aqs due date to a phrase, keeping its time unless the phrase gives one
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit postpone\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIR\fR> [\fIPHRASE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move a task\*(Aqs due date to a phrase, keeping its time unless the phrase gives one
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object per result, with `"v":1`, instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI colors
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIR\fR>
A row number, id prefix or title words
.TP
[\fIPHRASE\fR]
A date phrase, default `tomorrow`: `fri`, `in 3 days`, `next week`, `9am`
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  orbit postpone 1
  orbit postpone 3f2b9c fri
  orbit postpone buy milk "in 3 days" \-\-dry\-run
